-- outer: a module that imports another module (§13.13 recursion).
-- Its own import of inner propagates the ambient suffix: whatever
-- suffix outer was imported with, inner's atoms are mangled with it
-- too. The bytesBind of InnerMod mangles, so the handle and the
-- import's reference to it stay consistent within the module.
: [bytesBind InnerMod "inner"; import InnerMod Nil []]

(Go, reply) : lob reply (OuterHi,)
